WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:11.820
Welcome to DBL Group’s TalentHub!

2
00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:17.942
Do you need to raise a requisition to
recruit new manpower for your unit?

3
00:00:18.262 --> 00:00:22.422
Then this tutorial is for you.

4
00:00:22.542 --> 00:00:26.490
Today, we’ll walk through
how to create a requisition,

5
00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:30.810
what happens after submission, and what to
do if it gets returned. Let’s get started!

6
00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:38.670
First, let’s see how to sign in to
TalentHub. You don’t need to select

7
00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:43.790
or request a separate role to
become a requisition raiser.

8
00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:48.910
Once the Head of Talent Acquisition
assigns you as a raiser for your unit

9
00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:54.150
in Approval Paths, the required access
becomes available in your account.

10
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.420
To sign in,
enter your official DBL email address.

11
00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:02.540
Then enter your password.

12
00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:08.340
If you’re using your own computer,
you can select the Remember me option.

13
00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:13.700
This keeps your email address filled in
for your next login. Now click Sign in.

14
00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:18.490
Remember the paper Employee
Requisition Form you used to fill out?

15
00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:24.357
You can now complete the same
process digitally through TalentHub.

16
00:01:24.477 --> 00:01:29.929
Your main responsibility is to
provide the position details

17
00:01:30.049 --> 00:01:35.610
and specify which facilities
the new employee will need.

18
00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:40.930
The remaining steps will be
handled by the responsible teams.

19
00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:44.440
After signing in,
you’ll see your Dashboard.

20
00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:49.160
The main navigation menu is on the left.
Here you’ll find options such as

21
00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:54.080
Dashboard, Requisitions, Organogram,
Employees, and Notifications.

22
00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:59.430
Now let’s understand your
responsibilities as a requisition raiser.

23
00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:05.830
You don’t need to select approvers
when creating a requisition.

24
00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:12.190
You also won’t approve your own
requisition. Reviewing candidates’ CVs

25
00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:18.710
isn’t part of this role either. Your main
responsibility is to create requisitions

26
00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:24.470
with accurate information and update them
when necessary. As a requisition raiser,

27
00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:29.848
most of your work will happen in the
Requisitions section. Let’s open it.

28
00:02:32.698 --> 00:02:38.658
Now let’s create a new requisition.
The form is divided into just two steps.

29
00:02:38.778 --> 00:02:44.698
In the first step, you’ll enter the
position details. In the second,

30
00:02:44.818 --> 00:02:50.897
you’ll specify the facilities required
for the new employee. The entire

31
00:02:51.017 --> 00:02:56.538
process usually takes around five minutes.
Start by clicking Requisitions.

32
00:02:56.888 --> 00:03:00.288
At the top,
you’ll notice several summary tiles.

33
00:03:00.408 --> 00:03:06.328
These show how many requisitions
you have at different stages.

34
00:03:06.448 --> 00:03:10.088
Below them is the
detailed requisition list.

35
00:03:10.208 --> 00:03:15.448
To create a new one, click the New
requisition button on the right.

36
00:03:15.798 --> 00:03:19.198
Now take a look at the form.

37
00:03:19.318 --> 00:03:25.038
At the top,
Raising as already displays your name.

38
00:03:25.158 --> 00:03:31.439
Similarly, Unit / Factory is
prefilled with your assigned unit.

39
00:03:31.559 --> 00:03:37.092
If you’re authorized to raise
requisitions for multiple units,

40
00:03:37.212 --> 00:03:40.959
you can select the appropriate unit here.

41
00:03:41.799 --> 00:03:47.398
Next, choose the relevant
Line of Business.

42
00:03:47.748 --> 00:03:52.827
Next is the Department field.

43
00:03:52.947 --> 00:03:57.468
Select the department that
requires manpower. In our example,

44
00:03:57.588 --> 00:04:02.668
we’re raising a requisition for
the factory’s HR department.

45
00:04:03.108 --> 00:04:07.188
So we’ll select Plant HR. If there’s a
specific section, include that as well.

46
00:04:07.538 --> 00:04:12.618
Now select the required position under
Designation / Job title. For this example,

47
00:04:13.058 --> 00:04:18.378
we’re choosing Executive.
But suppose someone at the Officer

48
00:04:18.498 --> 00:04:23.698
or Senior Officer level could also
fill this position. In that case,

49
00:04:23.818 --> 00:04:29.098
click Add another designation and include
those additional titles. This allows

50
00:04:29.658 --> 00:04:34.898
you to specify multiple suitable
designations within the same requisition.

51
00:04:35.248 --> 00:04:40.541
Next is Requisition type. Here, you need
to specify why the manpower is required.

52
00:04:40.661 --> 00:04:45.689
If you’re adding headcount for
a new position, select New.

53
00:04:45.809 --> 00:04:51.129
If you’re hiring someone to replace an
employee who has left, select Replace.

54
00:04:51.249 --> 00:04:56.969
In our example,
we’re creating a replacement requisition.

55
00:04:57.089 --> 00:05:03.328
So we’ll select Replace.

56
00:05:03.678 --> 00:05:08.558
After selecting Replace,
a few additional fields will appear.

57
00:05:08.678 --> 00:05:14.678
First, use the Employee field to find
and select the employee being replaced.

58
00:05:14.798 --> 00:05:20.038
In our example, we’ll select Sadia Islam.

59
00:05:20.158 --> 00:05:26.198
Next, specify the reason for leaving.

60
00:05:26.318 --> 00:05:31.198
Here, we’re choosing Better Opportunity.

61
00:05:31.318 --> 00:05:37.398
If you’re replacing multiple employees,

62
00:05:37.518 --> 00:05:43.598
use Add another employee to include them.

63
00:05:43.948 --> 00:05:49.988
Now enter the number of employees
required under Nos. of required post.

64
00:05:50.108 --> 00:05:56.095
We need one employee, so we’ll enter 1.
Next to it is Total no. of vacant post.

65
00:05:56.215 --> 00:06:01.028
You don’t need to enter this manually.
The system automatically

66
00:06:01.148 --> 00:06:05.828
retrieves the vacant position count
from the organogram. This information

67
00:06:05.948 --> 00:06:11.548
helps determine whether the requirement
is for a new position or a replacement.

68
00:06:11.898 --> 00:06:16.818
Next, select the location where the new
employee will work under Place of posting.

69
00:06:16.938 --> 00:06:22.658
In our example,
we’ll choose Jinnat Complex.

70
00:06:23.258 --> 00:06:28.058
Then enter the date the position
became vacant under Vacant date.

71
00:06:28.778 --> 00:06:33.818
And under When needed,
specify when the new employee is required.

72
00:06:34.168 --> 00:06:37.248
Now set the requisition’s Priority.

73
00:06:37.368 --> 00:06:42.048
This indicates how urgently
the manpower is needed.

74
00:06:42.168 --> 00:06:48.368
For our example, we’ll select Moderate.
Next, choose the employment type.

75
00:06:48.488 --> 00:06:54.568
Is the position Permanent, Temporary, or
Contractual? Select the appropriate option

76
00:06:54.688 --> 00:06:59.368
and click Next. This takes us
to the second step of the form.

77
00:06:59.718 --> 00:07:04.118
We’ve now reached step two,
Facility Requirements.

78
00:07:04.238 --> 00:07:09.198
Here, you’ll specify the facilities the
new employee needs to perform their job.

79
00:07:09.478 --> 00:07:14.078
Remember to select only the facilities
that are genuinely required.

80
00:07:14.278 --> 00:07:20.118
For example, if the employee
needs a laptop or desktop,

81
00:07:20.238 --> 00:07:26.318
select Needed under Laptop / Desktop.
Then choose the required device.

82
00:07:26.438 --> 00:07:31.238
In our example, we’ll select Laptop.

83
00:07:31.588 --> 00:07:36.642
There’s something important to remember
about Transport and Dormitory facilities.

84
00:07:36.762 --> 00:07:42.669
Selecting these options doesn’t guarantee
that the employee will receive them.

85
00:07:43.349 --> 00:07:48.349
Transport availability depends on the
assigned route, schedule, and available

86
00:07:48.469 --> 00:07:54.309
seats. Similarly, dormitory accommodation
depends on vacancy and allocation.

87
00:07:54.429 --> 00:08:00.828
The form displays these conditions
before you select the facilities.

88
00:08:00.948 --> 00:08:03.498
So choose them according
to the actual requirements.

89
00:08:03.618 --> 00:08:09.738
Finally, let’s complete Seating
Arrangement. If the employee needs a

90
00:08:09.858 --> 00:08:15.858
seating arrangement, select Needed.
Then specify whether an existing seat is

91
00:08:15.978 --> 00:08:21.898
available or a new seat is required. In
our example, we’ll select Existing seat.

92
00:08:22.338 --> 00:08:27.378
Now review the form once more to make sure
everything is correct. When you’re ready,

93
00:08:27.498 --> 00:08:31.398
click Send for job analysis. That’s it!
Your requisition has been submitted.

94
00:08:34.208 --> 00:08:39.849
As you can see, the requisition
has been created successfully.

95
00:08:39.969 --> 00:08:46.129
The system has automatically assigned
it a unique requisition number.

96
00:08:46.249 --> 00:08:51.678
Its current status is Job Analysis. This
means the requisition is now with your

97
00:08:51.798 --> 00:08:55.398
unit’s Factory HR team. They’ve already
received a notification about it.

98
00:08:58.018 --> 00:09:03.018
You might be wondering what happens
after submitting a requisition.

99
00:09:03.138 --> 00:09:08.378
Here’s something important to remember.
The requisition doesn’t go

100
00:09:08.498 --> 00:09:13.659
directly to the approvers. It first
goes to your unit’s Factory HR team.

101
00:09:13.779 --> 00:09:19.538
They review the position requirements
and complete the job analysis.

102
00:09:19.888 --> 00:09:23.608
The Factory HR team will complete
Section B of the requisition.

103
00:09:24.288 --> 00:09:28.888
This includes the job responsibilities,
required qualifications,

104
00:09:29.008 --> 00:09:32.968
experience, and other relevant details.

105
00:09:33.568 --> 00:09:39.848
They’ll also attach the
detailed Job Description, or JD.

106
00:09:39.968 --> 00:09:44.688
Any changes made during this stage
will be recorded in the system history.

107
00:09:45.038 --> 00:09:49.481
Once Factory HR submits the job analysis,
the approval process begins.

108
00:09:49.601 --> 00:09:54.881
To follow this process, open the Approvals
tab. Here, you can see who is responsible

109
00:09:55.001 --> 00:10:00.441
for approving the requisition. You’ll
also be able to see who has approved it,

110
00:10:00.561 --> 00:10:06.158
when they approved it,
and whether they left any comments.

111
00:10:06.508 --> 00:10:08.628
Take a look at the approval chain.

112
00:10:08.748 --> 00:10:14.788
The requisition moves through the
assigned approvers one by one.

113
00:10:14.908 --> 00:10:20.268
Each approver reviews the requisition and
makes a decision at their assigned level.

114
00:10:20.388 --> 00:10:24.028
This is how the approvals are
completed in the predefined order.

115
00:10:24.378 --> 00:10:29.618
Here’s another useful thing to know.
When you create a requisition,

116
00:10:29.738 --> 00:10:34.899
its assigned approval chain is
saved with that requisition.

117
00:10:35.019 --> 00:10:39.219
Even if Approval Paths are changed later,

118
00:10:39.339 --> 00:10:43.539
the approval chain of an existing
requisition remains unchanged.

119
00:10:43.979 --> 00:10:49.338
This ensures that each requisition follows
its originally assigned approval process.

120
00:10:49.688 --> 00:10:55.888
Now let’s understand the
different requisition statuses.

121
00:10:56.008 --> 00:11:02.208
Job Analysis means Factory HR is
preparing the position details.

122
00:11:02.328 --> 00:11:08.368
Pending Approval means the requisition
is going through the approval process.

123
00:11:08.488 --> 00:11:14.288
Approved means all required approvals
are complete. Profile Ready means

124
00:11:14.408 --> 00:11:20.848
the role profile has been prepared.
Posted means the job advertisement is live

125
00:11:21.767 --> 00:11:28.048
on the careers page. And Rejected
means the requisition was not approved.

126
00:11:28.168 --> 00:11:32.888
These statuses help you track exactly
where your requisition stands.

127
00:11:35.738 --> 00:11:40.658
Now let’s see what to do if
your requisition gets returned.

128
00:11:41.458 --> 00:11:45.108
This usually happens in two situations.
The first is when Factory HR needs

129
00:11:45.498 --> 00:11:51.777
additional information about something
you’ve submitted. In that case, you’ll

130
00:11:51.897 --> 00:11:58.058
receive a notification. Click the bell
icon at the top and open the notification.

131
00:11:58.408 --> 00:12:03.528
When you open the requisition from the
notification, you’ll see a note in the

132
00:12:03.648 --> 00:12:09.515
Job Analysis tab. Factory HR will explain
which information needs to be corrected.

133
00:12:09.635 --> 00:12:15.408
Notice that the main requisition status
remains Job Analysis. The requisition

134
00:12:15.768 --> 00:12:21.368
has simply been returned to you
temporarily for the required correction.

135
00:12:21.718 --> 00:12:25.598
To make the correction,
click Edit details.

136
00:12:26.118 --> 00:12:30.998
You can update the necessary
information from here.

137
00:12:31.118 --> 00:12:36.718
In our example,
we need to correct the Vacant date.

138
00:12:36.998 --> 00:12:41.238
So we’ll select the correct date. Then
click Save changes to save the update.

139
00:12:41.588 --> 00:12:46.228
Once you’ve made the correction,
click Resend for job analysis.

140
00:12:46.348 --> 00:12:51.629
The requisition will return to the
Factory HR team. They’ll receive another

141
00:12:51.749 --> 00:12:57.428
notification and continue the process
using the updated information.

142
00:12:57.778 --> 00:13:02.698
Now let’s look at the second situation.
Suppose your requisition is already in the

143
00:13:02.818 --> 00:13:06.698
approval stage. But one of the
approvers needs additional information.

144
00:13:07.298 --> 00:13:11.578
They can select Need more info. This
temporarily stops the approval process

145
00:13:12.258 --> 00:13:17.018
and returns the requisition to you.

146
00:13:17.138 --> 00:13:22.858
To see what information is required,
open the Approvals tab.

147
00:13:23.218 --> 00:13:28.018
You’ll find the approver’s comments
under Sent back to you for clarification.

148
00:13:28.368 --> 00:13:33.328
Read the approver’s comments carefully.

149
00:13:33.448 --> 00:13:39.688
If any information needs to be changed,
update it through Edit details.

150
00:13:39.808 --> 00:13:44.407
Then click Send for approval.
Here’s something important to remember.

151
00:13:44.527 --> 00:13:49.768
After resubmission, the approval chain
starts again from the first level. This

152
00:13:49.888 --> 00:13:54.848
means every approver gets the opportunity
to review the corrected requisition.

153
00:13:55.198 --> 00:14:00.838
You may also be wondering what
happens if a requisition is Rejected.

154
00:14:00.958 --> 00:14:06.118
If an approver rejects it,
that requisition’s process ends.

155
00:14:06.878 --> 00:14:11.158
You can find the rejection
reason in the Approvals tab.

156
00:14:11.918 --> 00:14:17.398
If the manpower is still required,
you’ll need to create a new requisition.

157
00:14:18.078 --> 00:14:23.638
Also, there’s no option to withdraw
a submitted requisition yourself.

158
00:14:24.158 --> 00:14:26.278
So if the position is no longer needed,

159
00:14:26.398 --> 00:14:29.718
inform the person currently
responsible for it.

160
00:14:33.488 --> 00:14:37.369
Now let’s see what happens after
the requisition is approved.

161
00:14:37.809 --> 00:14:43.689
Once all assigned approvers
have completed their approvals,

162
00:14:44.269 --> 00:14:48.369
the status changes to Approved. The role
profile for the position is then prepared.

163
00:14:48.489 --> 00:14:53.889
Once the profile is ready,
the status changes to Profile Ready.

164
00:14:54.009 --> 00:14:58.608
You’ll also receive notifications
about these important updates.

165
00:14:58.958 --> 00:15:02.318
After approval,

166
00:15:02.438 --> 00:15:06.358
the Head of Talent Acquisition
oversees the next steps of recruitment.

167
00:15:06.478 --> 00:15:11.438
They decide which sources will be
used to collect candidates’ CVs.

168
00:15:11.558 --> 00:15:16.998
They also assign a Corporate Recruiter
to manage the recruitment process.

169
00:15:17.118 --> 00:15:22.278
The assigned recruiter coordinates
the process through to onboarding.

170
00:15:22.398 --> 00:15:28.078
You’ll also be notified when the
job advertisement is published.

171
00:15:28.428 --> 00:15:33.348
Here’s a small but useful tip.
Before creating a requisition,

172
00:15:33.468 --> 00:15:38.708
you can check the position counts and
vacancies in the organogram. This gives

173
00:15:38.828 --> 00:15:43.308
you a clearer understanding of the
current staffing situation in your unit.

174
00:15:46.158 --> 00:15:50.358
Now let’s see how notifications
work in TalentHub.

175
00:15:50.478 --> 00:15:55.478
There are several ways to stay
informed about important updates.

176
00:15:55.598 --> 00:16:00.878
First, the bell icon at the top shows
the number of new notifications.

177
00:16:00.998 --> 00:16:07.398
Second, when an update arrives,
you’ll hear a short notification sound

178
00:16:07.518 --> 00:16:12.958
and see an on-screen message. And here’s
something convenient: the page you’re

179
00:16:13.078 --> 00:16:17.918
working on can update automatically.
So you don’t need to keep refreshing it.

180
00:16:18.268 --> 00:16:23.708
To view all your notifications in
one place, click Notifications.

181
00:16:23.828 --> 00:16:29.540
Here, you’ll find important updates
related to your requisitions. For example,

182
00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:35.229
when a requisition is returned, additional
information is requested, or a requisition

183
00:16:35.349 --> 00:16:41.468
is approved or rejected. These important
notifications are also sent to your email.

184
00:16:41.818 --> 00:16:48.018
You can also choose whether to
receive email notifications.

185
00:16:48.138 --> 00:16:52.338
To change this, open Settings.
Then go to the Notifications tab.

186
00:16:52.458 --> 00:16:57.258
Here, you can turn Email notifications on
or off according to your preference.

187
00:17:00.108 --> 00:17:04.548
Now let’s answer a few
frequently asked questions.

188
00:17:05.068 --> 00:17:10.868
First, why can’t I see my unit
in the Unit / Factory list?

189
00:17:11.468 --> 00:17:16.628
This happens when you haven’t
been assigned as a requisition

190
00:17:16.748 --> 00:17:22.948
raiser for that unit in Approval Paths.
In this situation,

191
00:17:23.068 --> 00:17:26.868
contact your unit’s Factory HR team
or the Head of Talent Acquisition.

192
00:17:27.548 --> 00:17:30.828
They can help you
resolve the access issue.

193
00:17:31.178 --> 00:17:37.218
Another common question is what to do
if you see Approval path not found.

194
00:17:38.058 --> 00:17:43.378
This means the approval chain for the
relevant unit hasn’t been properly

195
00:17:43.498 --> 00:17:49.618
configured or saved. In this case, contact
your unit’s Factory HR team or the Head of

196
00:17:49.738 --> 00:17:55.298
Talent Acquisition. You might also
wonder who can modify your requisition.

197
00:17:55.418 --> 00:18:01.618
Depending on the workflow,
Factory HR and the person currently

198
00:18:01.738 --> 00:18:07.098
responsible for the requisition
can make authorized changes.

199
00:18:07.448 --> 00:18:12.448
Another question: can you view
candidates’ CVs as a requisition raiser?

200
00:18:12.968 --> 00:18:18.168
Generally, no. Candidate
management isn’t part of this role.

201
00:18:18.288 --> 00:18:23.808
However, if you’re invited to
participate in an interview panel,

202
00:18:23.928 --> 00:18:29.048
you’ll find the relevant interview
information under My Interviews.

203
00:18:31.898 --> 00:18:36.458
For more detailed information about
TalentHub, visit the Tutorials section.

204
00:18:36.578 --> 00:18:41.858
You’ll find the complete guide there in
PDF format. For access-related issues,

205
00:18:41.978 --> 00:18:47.178
contact your unit’s Factory HR team
or the Head of Talent Acquisition.

206
00:18:47.298 --> 00:18:53.058
For login-related problems,
contact the IT Helpdesk.

207
00:18:53.498 --> 00:18:56.858
Thank you for using DBL Group’s TalentHub.

